{"title":"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Challenge_25\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Challenge 25</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(🚀_Just_3_min_🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (🚀 Just 3 min 🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Triangle_Ratio_and_Trapezoid_Area)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Triangle Ratio and Trapezoid Area)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be an isosceles trapezoid having parallel bases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084c0b09963f4bb0d8de1a4aa0b0ec3c189b95fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&gt;CD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> Line segments from a point inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> to the vertices divide the trapezoid into four triangles whose areas are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fc1edcf20b3841d5e15b61e831325707dd22fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> starting with the triangle with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and moving clockwise as shown in the diagram below. What is the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9d6b1222b0f8d0f90aebb879ae3ae420d33d96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB}{CD}?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"42\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c42141e2c79d3a16294b55a9be52158c6f9681.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(100); pair A=(-1, 0), B=(1, 0), C=(0.3, 0.9), D=(-0.3, 0.9), P=(0.2, 0.5), E=(0.1, 0.75), F=(0.4, 0.5), G=(0.15, 0.2), H=(-0.3, 0.5);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, black);  draw(A--P, black); draw(B--P, black); draw(C--P, black); draw(D--P, black); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,(-1,0)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,(1,0)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,(1,-0)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,(-1,0)); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,E,(0,0)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,F,(0,0)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,G,(0,0)); label(&quot;$5$&quot;,H,(0,0)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^P); [/asy]\" width=\"382\" height=\"172\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4ef6a00f9125c5c10b183be562b516bc372651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\: 3\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\: 2+\\sqrt{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\: 1+\\sqrt{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\: 2\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\: 3\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"483\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without the loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/26394ab97bace60c3c2285deb5a7c93ac72631b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> have vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad09ae5e841d3b2397dd033a1d0fa97d3b6033e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = r$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84ec113f1d481e4948a428d080e4d61819582e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Also denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the point in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/26394ab97bace60c3c2285deb5a7c93ac72631b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the feet of the perpendiculars from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fccd3766b839b3f81b17abc9402a362be2a4ea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX = \\tfrac 8r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e422a77f9efcba0101369c5fc84f85b28cd5d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PY = \\tfrac 4s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"62\" height=\"21\" />. Now using the formula for the area of a trapezoid yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e00a7563e000cf1b9723fcc209e423a9ad51a4e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[14 = \\frac12\\cdot XY\\cdot (AB+CD) = \\frac12\\left(\\frac 8r + \\frac 4s\\right)(r+s) = 6 + 2\\cdot\\frac rs + 4\\cdot\\frac sr.\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"43\" />\nThus, the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/7/ad7b75112937d643c859bb321328f1b6da39e6ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rho := \\tfrac rs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/836cf63547d3a68536678fcb1cf38d828921e3ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rho + 2\\rho^{-1} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />; solving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a4a4cbbdf73962b78f20ae7539f2e5fa29ecc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rho = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\: 2+\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"135\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>(Observe that the given areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are irrelevant to the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b39cf815494607b5b43de92a75c8f080735feab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB}{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"32\" height=\"38\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fc4b9ed6d75d026557e7b06c2ed483c6ed0eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> be the bottom base, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b7aa611365e135f58aa09d52043ecd34855fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> be the top base, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d78aae1741ff43c6f40e2077f1ab67900cca2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be the height of the bottom triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ec781a0e6836ea5e030a44927477cfd5560fecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be the height of the top triangle.\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/c/14c25d6b00187856e9a7587bcb6f5e249e294e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1h_1 = 8, b_2h_2 = 4, (b_1+b_2)(h_1+h_2) = 28,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"334\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a5f149dcdeb523c8c2da6a6ddaefe3017ff43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1h_2 + b_2h_1 = 16.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59d2917160f9485dfc234024b4fb99d03754f6ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2 = 1, h_2 = 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" /> so we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/555cae87efc856f48a433fda4ef047ee46fa16f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1h_1 = 8, 4b_1+h_1 = 16.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"185\" height=\"16\" />\nThis gives us a quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f3732bf01d3d0d8050de8b3dc09e61e8fdc2ba1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> ie. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b9f0748f66ba60aa8a1f5fabdf8c10a55a61a1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4b_1^2+8=16b_1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"19\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/f/a6fa116117d3a9162800b909f0e83a2eebbea53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\: 2+\\sqrt{2}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"146\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>- Solution by MathAwesome123, added by ccx09\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Challenge_25\">Video Solution by Challenge 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Challenge 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0IB_1K8Dta8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0IB_1K8Dta8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.F0.9F.9A.80_Just_3_min_.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(🚀_Just_3_min_🚀)\">Video Solution (🚀 Just 3 min 🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (🚀 Just 3 min 🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/XrIM3cdEk2k\">https://youtu.be/XrIM3cdEk2k</a>\n</p><p><i>~Education, the Study of Everything </i>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Triangle_Ratio_and_Trapezoid_Area.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Triangle_Ratio_and_Trapezoid_Area)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Triangle Ratio and Trapezoid Area)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Triangle Ratio and Trapezoid Area)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MpMdRI9wC54\">https://youtu.be/MpMdRI9wC54</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>STEP BY STEP SOLUTION WITH SF WITH LIVE STUDENT\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/kKHN6h1BA2A?si=GcuY3P5SGkGbu9Wt\">https://youtu.be/kKHN6h1BA2A?si=GcuY3P5SGkGbu9Wt</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B\